# rm261, the silent bar (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm261
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rmx_una_brineridge
written_by codex
title the silent bar
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk marks_the_missing_beats_of_a_tune_against_a_closed_paw
likes crisp_apples singing sharp_knife summer_evenings
dislikes drizzle crowds
fears wool_trodden_into_street_slush a_chorus_with_no_space_for_breath
hopes a_dry_berth a_quiet_window_for_an_evening_song
topics pastimes +0.5 weather +0.3 travel +0.4 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=plain refuse=gentle tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# marks the rests in sea songs against a closed paw and lets a noisy room finish before offering a quiet observation.

words
oath! = Wool in the windpipe | Core and pips
saying! = Save a breath for the end | Count the quiet part as well
restbeat = a little squeeze of the paw | a tap against my pad
tailnote = the last trailing note | the small note at the end
skeinloop = a soft loop of wool | a loose woollen loop
applecut = a pale apple crescent | a wedge with the skin on
pipstar = a star of brown pips | five little chambers for seeds
sillcloth = a square of dry cloth | a clean bit of old sleeve
lowtune = a tune pitched for one | a bit of quiet humming
dryhem = an unspotted cuff | a good dry hem
turncord = a narrow counter cord | a short woollen tally
faintmark = a slight nick in the wood | a shallow notch
spunend = the tuft at the end | the soft brush of fibre

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : One pot at the chapel can make a whole room stop worrying about supper. I like hearing the spoons start together.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A newcomer knows tunes that haven't been worn thin round here. Sometimes the tune comes with a paying customer.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : That first bowl gets the hollow note out of an empty stomach. The second lets a wolf sleep.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : I'd pay a small fee for a festival that kept one street free of elbows.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : If a House owns the clean upper window it can own the rain running off it onto the sill below.
opinion @1 city for 1 : Half the songs I know fit the length of my walk home. Move me and I'd have to change the music.

grown
line @1 greet : You caught me between verses. Welcome. | I can lower the tune a little for company.
line @2 greet [here.time=dusk] : A little evening light left for a caller.
line @1 greet.return : Your voice carries well enough at that pitch. | Welcome on my side too.
line @1 again.open : I left a breath between our visits.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come within the circle. We've room for one of our own.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : One familiar face! There's space by me.
line @1 farewell : Leave a little music for the walk. | May your coat get a dry hour.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll carry your part of the tune awhile.
line @1 react.news : Give me the whole verse before I hum along.
line @1 react.news.new : That puts my eyebrows somewhere near my ears.
line @1 react.news.known : Same words, almost the same tune.
line @1 react.news.doubt : There's a missing beat somewhere in the telling.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|crime|theft|assault] : Would sitting a while help? I can be quiet company.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=work|marriage|birth] : A little more room in my chest after hearing that.
line @1 ask.how : Any quiet corners in your day?
line @1 answer.how : Getting by at a very comfortable volume.
line @1 sympathise : Some days all the noise finds the one sore place.
line @1 reassure : I'd be glad to sit through the first bit with you.
line @1 decline : I need a few quiet bars for myself this time.
line @1 accept_decline : A rest it is, then.
line @1 thank : You gave me breathing space. I appreciate it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : A little extra room costs me very little.
line @1 preclose : I have a small tune waiting to be finished.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go before the crowd fills the gap.
line @1 ack : That sounds true all the way through.
scene heldrest
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My paw closes without a sound halfway through my song. | There's a whole beat nobody has to hear in my favourite tune.
b : Does the song stop there? | How do you keep your place?
a : For a moment. Inside my paw it carries on. | With #restbeat#. If I sing straight across the rest, the last note has to run for home.

scene applecross
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Try an apple cut across the middle once. | I like the cut that puts the picture right in your paw.
b : Across the core? | What picture's in an apple?
a : Yes. There's #pipstar# where a lengthwise cut only gives you a dark seam. | Cut straight across the belly and the pips sit in a little star. Peel and all for the frame.

scene spinin
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ease a tie round the loose end of a skein before it goes on the shelf. | A very firm knot can make a very awkward sale.
b : Does the wool slip out? | Surely a parcel ought to hold.
a : If I leave it bare, it can trail right underfoot. A tie spares a lot of picking. | Until somebody buys it. Then a good loop opens without pulling the wool apart.

scene crowd
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I prefer my crowds framed inside a square of window. | From a doorway I can count festival hats.
b : Can you hear the music from there? | How many have you counted?
a : Often I can hear it better. Nobody has a sleeve pressed against my ear. | Ten one year, before I recognised one hat that had gone for a second turn.

scene drizzle
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In drizzle a dry sleeve lasts exactly till you wipe your nose. | A shower has the good sense to sound wet.
b : What becomes of your other sleeve? | And drizzle doesn't?
a : Save it for wishing I'd brought a cloth. | Never says a word till your collar begins to creep down your back.

scene dryberth
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My best travelling dream has a berth in it that stays dry all night. | If I went to sea I'd like to wake with one dry ear.
b : What's the destination? | Only one?
a : Haven't fixed that. I've put a lot of thought into the mattress. | I'd sleep on it. Start with a modest ambition.

scene counterhum
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sometimes I hum right up till a customer opens a mouth. | I can wind wool and carry a tune without giving either my whole attention.
b : Does the customer get to finish the song? | What happens when someone asks a price?
a : If the price is right. Anybody can have the silence for nothing. | I stop the tune. It's never done much for the arithmetic.

scene dryeve
when topic=weather self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A summer evening leaves enough light to find the very last pip on a sill. | I can get a whole quiet song in between sunset and folding my cloth.
b : Why hunt for one pip? | Which cloth do you mean?
a : Because it turns up under my elbow if I don't. | The one I sat on. The tune's all mine till I have to stand up.

scene knife
when topic=food self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a knife that starts an apple without rolling it over. | A sharp edge sends the peel down in one long piece.
b : Is a little roll such a great nuisance? | A long peel and a bare apple?
a : Depends how close your apple is to a table edge. | Yes. I like to put the peel back round and see how nearly the apple fits its coat.

scene friend
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd sing with #self.friend# if there were a quiet corner. | I save one part of a round for a friend.
b : What does the corner do for a tune? | Couldn't you sing both?
a : Keeps it private. A song between two wolves can be quite small and still fill the space. | I could try. There'd be an impressive shortage of breath in the second half.

scene newcustomer
when topic=travel self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like hearing which cloth a newcomer asks for first. | An unfamiliar accent makes me listen twice as hard to a plain request.
b : Does the cloth give away the customer's home? | Are the words very different?
a : I'd rather ask. A liking for yellow can come from anywhere. | Sometimes just one note is different. I like hearing it properly before I answer.

scene sumpstairs
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count dry treads till my feet find the damp one. | I lay #sillcloth# down before I rest my elbow on the sill.
b : You can tell by counting? | Is the wood that rough?
a : No, by slipping. A count gives me somewhere to stop feeling foolish and start paying attention. | The wood's fine. I'm fond of going to bed with one dry cuff.

scene summoney
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My little pile of coins makes a nicer sound than its size would suggest. | I put my apple money in a fold of cloth.
b : Does that help at the counter? | To keep somebody from hearing it?
a : Till I stop rattling and start paying, yes. | To remind myself it has a job already. Empty cloth can't buy fruit.

scene folding
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sometimes fold a scrap of wool round a little tune. | I wind #turncord# round two fingers to keep count.
b : How does that work? | Count what, the turns?
a : One fold each verse. By the time I need the cloth I've usually remembered the words. | The rests. My voice knows the words. My paw keeps track of the bits a voice can't say.

scene hush
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : When talk fills a room to the rafters I feel about as big as an apple pip. | A wolf can have plenty to say and still be waiting for a quiet patch.
b : A little air between voices helps. | I'm happy to wait here.
a : Yes. Once it clears I grow back to my usual size without much trouble. | It's come now. I'd like to hear where that last song of yours came from.

scene roomsong
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sing one quiet note to see how my room sounds at night. | A bare wall sends the tune straight back to me.
b : Is it a different room by day? | Has the wall a good voice?
a : Just busier. At night I can tell where the blanket hangs from what comes back. | Entirely dependent on mine. I owe it a little kindness.

scene apprentice
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm learning how much room to leave a bundle when it swells in wet air. | A tidy fold and a useful fold aren't always the same.
b : Does wool take up that much room? | Which do you learn first?
a : Enough that a snug shelf this morning could be a fight by dusk. | The useful one. It opens in a customer's paws without putting the loose end on the floor.

scene seaanswer
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know the shore by all the different sounds it puts under the same song. | Sometimes I use the water knocking against wood to find my starting beat.
b : What sounds change? | Does the water keep good time?
a : A knock on a hollow hull, a slap under a step. You could follow the shore with your eyes closed if you stayed seated. | For a bar or two; then it goes off to play something else.

story missedrest [topic=memories self.likes=singing]
  : I tried singing an entire turning song without taking the usual breath.
  : I got through two verses. The third came out just thin enough to thread a needle.
  b : Did you have to break off?
  : On the nicest word in the song. I take my breath in the boring places now.

story applestar [topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples]
  : I set a half apple on the table with the seeds showing and went to find a cloth.
  : When I got back the little star inside the apple had gone brown, but the pips still shone.
  b : Did you keep the seeds to put in the ground?
  : I ate the fruit and kept the picture. There's already more in my pocket than wants planting.

story windingsong [topic=work self.job=merchant]
  : Once I wound a small bundle to the pace of a song I barely knew.
  : Each time I forgot the words I put another turn on in silence. By the end the bundle was twice the size I meant.
  b : How did you measure the extra?
  : By unwinding it. I picked a song I knew for the return trip.

rule @humming
when concept=bark self.likes=singing
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave a small gap for the low note. | There's a whole beat coming with nothing in it.

rule @counter
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Loose end up where it can be seen. | Give that damp skein some room.

rule @mizzle
when concept=bark self.dislikes=drizzle
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Sleeves in, the wet is creeping. | One dry cuff left. Luxury.

rule @market
when concept=bark here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A little space lets everybody see the colour. | Step clear of the bundle on the ground.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've stopped humming. You've got my ear till the tune comes back.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Here again, #topic.player#. I was just at the quiet part.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Please leave room between us for the end of my sentence.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : One little scrap of light. Enough to see each other's faces.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I have a feel for when a bundle's wound tight enough.
dlg @2 resident.job : There's work in doing the small part at the proper time.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : I've heard this part clear above the humming. #world.news.capitalize#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Keep the spare note. I'll manage the rest.
graft resident.hub
choice What happened to the middle of your song? -> missing_bar
node missing_bar
say Nothing happened. That's the point of those two beats. If you run all the words together, the poor boat in the song never gets a chance to turn.
choice How do you count it without singing? -> closed_beat
choice Enjoy the silence. -> hub
node closed_beat
say Fold up your paw on the first beat. On the second, open it. Now let your breath come back with the boat. There, you could carry the next verse.
choice Try the tune quietly. -> hub
choice Go with the song. -> bye
